The activation family in one pass and in int16: SIGMOID, SILU and SWIGLU (lab proposal)

The elementwise family is 114 ms of the 536 ms of DSP op time of a 512-token prefill of the 4B
(measured 2026-09-20), and SWIGLU, SIGMOID and SILU are most of it. Two costs make it that
large, and this proposal removes both.

The first is the evaluation. hvx_vec_fast_sigmoid_f32 is a chain of about 25 qfloat operations,
of which 14 are multiplies, and hvx_vec_inverse_f32 holds 6 of those on its own. A v79 packet
holds one qfloat multiply and a result is ready two packets after its producer, thus the chain
cannot fill the machine whatever the compiler does. hvx-act-i16.h evaluates the same functions
as a piecewise polynomial in int16 read by vlut16: a packet holds two int16 multiplies or four
integer adds, and the routine works on two vectors at once so no packet waits for its producer.

The second is the number of passes. silu_f32 and swiglu_f32 call the sigmoid over the whole row
and then walk the row again to multiply, thus each element is loaded two or four times where
once is enough. A v79 packet holds one load and one store, thus the pass count is the memory
cost. The kernels here read each input once and write the output once.

The forms keep the sign and the linear part in the float domain, where they are exact, and
never compute a small result as the difference of two near-equal numbers:

  sigmoid(x) = x < 0 ? g(|x|) : 1 - g(|x|)   g(u) = 1 / (1 + e^u)
  silu(x)    = relu(x) - h(|x|)              h(u) = u / (1 + e^u)
  swiglu     = silu(x0) * x1

tools/htp-lab/gen/act_i16.py generates the header and its --check mode reports the error. A new
activation needs one entry of its FUNCS table and no new code.

